# Kimi Code second (tier 2)

After **Grok Build** (tier 1, `.cursor/rules/grok-build-first.mdc`) hits its
weekly limit or quota, **remaining coding automation goes through Kimi Code
CLI** until Kimi usage runs out. Then use **Cursor** (tier 3).

## Tier 2 — Kimi Code CLI (K3)

1. Run `scripts/dev/kimi-preflight.sh` (or `scripts/dev/agent-coding-preflight.sh`).
2. Delegate coding:

   ```bash
   scripts/dev/kimi-headless.sh -p "<task>"
   ```

   Model is pinned to **K3** (`-m kimi-code/k3`, `--output-format stream-json`
   added by the wrapper when omitted).

3. **Auth order:** `kimi login` (device OAuth) on the VM, else Runtime Secret
   `KIMI_MODEL_API_KEY` (+ optional `KIMI_MODEL_NAME`, `KIMI_MODEL_BASE_URL`).
   Plain `KIMI_API_KEY` is ignored. Surface the login URL and code immediately
   when OAuth is required.

## When to leave tier 2 (tier 3 — Cursor)

Use **Cursor Agent** when Kimi returns payment/quota/auth errors, when
`kimi-preflight.sh` fails with no OAuth and no `KIMI_MODEL_API_KEY`, or when
headless `-p` cannot proceed. **Security testing and red-team passes** use
**Grok 4.7** inside Cursor when available; other Cursor work uses Composer /
auto.

Record tier and reason in the PR **Provenance** section and
`docs/audit/2026-10-provenance.md`. Operator detail:
`docs/operators/kimi-code-cloud.md`, `.cursor/kimi-code.md`.
